/**

    @mainpage CivilCvCAD Source Documentation

    @section toc Table of Contents
    - @ref intro_main "Introduction"
    - @ref organization "Organization of the API Documentation"
    - @ref asyncrecompute "Async recompute threading rules"
    - @ref other_doc "Other Documentation"

    @section intro_main Introduction

    This is the source documentation of CivilCvCAD. It
    is automatically generated from the source code and describes the different
    components of the CivilCvCAD source code, for both the parts written in C++
    and Python.  The next section discusses the organization of this API
    documentation and the last section describes other forms of documentation
    that CivilCvCAD has.

    @section organization Organization of the API Documentation

    This documentation is divided into several topics of which the most important are:
    - @ref CORE "Core"
      - @ref BASE "Base"
      - @ref APP "App"
      - @ref GUI "Gui"
    - @ref WORKBENCHES "Workbenches"
    - @ref EMBEDDED "Embedded 3rd party packages"

    Firstly, topic @ref CORE "Core" contains the core namespaces and classes
    that all of CivilCvCAD relies on.  This consists of namespace %Base (see topic
    @ref BASE "Base") that contains fundamental base classes, the namespace
    %App (see topic @ref APP "App") that contains classes for CivilCvCAD in
    command-line mode, and namespace %Gui (see topic @ref GUI "Gui") that
    contains the classes for CivilCvCAD's GUI.

    CivilCvCAD is highly modular and most of its functionality is within modules
    that are called @ref WORKBENCHES "Workbenches". Workbenches can be written
    in C++ or Python or in a combination of the two. Local workbenches can be
    installed from trusted offline media.

    Finally, there is the topic @ref EMBEDDED "Embedded 3rd party packages"
    that contains 3rd-party software of which the source is embedded in
    CivilCvCAD.  This means that during compilation, these packages will be
    compiled and linked to CivilCvCAD as opposed to non-embedded 3rd-party
    packages that are only linked to CivilCvCAD.  An example of an important
    non-embedded 3rd party software package is Open CASCADE Technology.

    @section other_doc Other Documentation

    General application help is resolved only from locally installed
    documentation. Build this source documentation locally to browse modules,
    classes, namespaces, source headers, and inheritance graphics.

  @if DEV_DOCUMENTATION

  @mainpage CivilCvCAD source documentation

    @image html civilcvcadsplash.png

    <b>Welcome to CivilCvCAD source documentation!</b>

    We hope you'll find it a convenient tool to explore, understand and
    experiment with the internals of the program.

    Being generated from the actual state of the code, this documentation
    is by no means a well structured corpus or a textbook, but more an
    utility to browse through the sources.

    For application help, use the locally installed documentation.

    CivilCvCAD being a fast moving target, don't hesitate to rebuild an up to
    date doc from source as often as needed (\ref makingdocs "more info"). CPU cycles are cheap
    nowadays!

    CivilCvCAD is distributed as an offline-only application.

  @endif

<small>
@GIT_REVISION_INFO@
</small>
 */

